From: RCTools GPU audit
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/kgsl: harden Channel old-kernel and headless paths

Base: lfdevs/mesa-for-android-container
Commit: 98f3d6229d61452cef80f8563af7c56ae599dc14

Changes:
* skip generic DRM PCI discovery when the explicit loader override is KGSL;
* require a real DRI3 X extension before the KGSL DRI3 fd shortcut;
* share the existing Turnip ION ABI definitions instead of duplicating them;
* fall back from dma-heap to either modern or legacy ION, including when the
  dma-heap node exists but allocation itself fails;
* close/free imported KGSL objects correctly on allocation/dup failures;
* avoid NULL dereferences after fd_bo_from_handle() failures;
* suppress only the misleading kcmp/DRM warning for explicitly selected KGSL.

The legacy ION sequence was validated on the real Channel 4.9 kernel with the
temporary compatibility shim.  Full device regression testing is still
required before replacing the known-good Mesa runtime.

